python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(x for row in grid for x in row)\n    color = next(x for x in counts if x not in (0, max(counts, key=counts.get)))\n    points = [(r, c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == color]\n    r0, c0 = min(r for r, c in points), min(c for r, c in points)\n    shape = {(r-r0, c-c0) for r, c in points}\n    rh, cw = max(r for r, c in shape)+1, max(c for r, c in shape)+1\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Copy the seed pattern to each location where it is supported by zeros.\n    for r in range(h-rh+1):\n        for c in range(w-cw+1):\n            if all(grid[r+dr][c+dc] == 0 for dr, dc in shape):\n                for dr, dc in shape:\n                    out[r+dr][c+dc] = color\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}}]}